\sqrt{3} \\end{bmatrix}.$</p>\n","topic":{"id":475,"name":"Defining Vector-Valued Functions"},"example":{"id":12452,"title":"Evaluating a Three-Component Vector-Valued Function"},"group":{"id":58478,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14253258,"answer":{"id":62316307,"cread":"2026-10-16T02:52:24.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":14823},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}}]},{"id":12451,"number":3,"title":"Finding the Magnitude of a Vector-Valued Function","answers":[{"id":62316323,"created":"2026-10-16T02:53:06.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":27845,"number":11,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 2:53 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:28","question":{"id":75004,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":12451,"text":"<p>Given that $\\mathbf r(t)  = \\left\\langle \\sqrt{t}, \\,  t-3 \\right\\rangle,$ $\\left|\\mathbf r\\left(5\\right)\\right|=$</p>\n","choice1":"$3$","choice2":"$5$","choice3":"$\\sqrt{3}$","choice4":"$\\sqrt{7}$","choice5":"$9$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>Evaluating the function at $t=5,$ we get</p>\n<p>\\begin{align*}\n\\mathbf r\\left(5\\right) &=\\left\\langle \\sqrt{5}, \\, 5-3\\right\\rangle \\\\[3pt]\n&=\\left\\langle \\sqrt{5} ,\\,2\\right\\rangle.\n\\end{align*}</p>\n<p>Computing the magnitude of this vector, we get</p>\n<p>\\begin{align*}\n\\left|\\mathbf r\\left(5\\right)\\right|&= \n\\sqrt{\\left(\\sqrt{5}\\right)^2 + \\left(2\\right)^2}\\\\[3pt]\n&=\\sqrt{5 + 4}\\\\[3pt]\n&=3.\n\\end{align*}</p>\n","topic":{"id":475,"name":"Defining Vector-Valued Functions"},"example":{"id":12451,"title":"Finding the Magnitude of a Vector-Valued Function"},"group":{"id":8809,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14253258,"answer":{"id":62316323,"cread":"2026-10-16T02:53:06.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":27845},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62316341,"created":"2026-10-16T02:53:42.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":null,"freeResponse":"[\"4\"]","timeElapsed":27584,"number":12,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 2:53 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:28","question":{"id":348682,"format":"FR","difficulty":1,"exampleId":12451,"text":"Given that $\\mathbf r(t)=\\left\\langle \\cos\\!\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi t}{2}\\right),\\, \\dfrac{4}{t-1} \\right\\rangle,$ what is $\\left|\\mathbf r(3)\\right|?$","choice1":null,"choice2":null,"choice3":null,"choice4":null,"choice5":null,"freeAnswerChoice":"\\newline\n\n$\\left|\\mathbf r(3)\\right| = $\n[\nanswer: 2;\n    type: number;\n    width: 35;\n    height: 20;\n    margin-left: 2;\n    margin-right: 1;\n    margin-top: 0;\n    margin-bottom: 0;\n    buttons: sqrt, frac;\n]","explanation":"<p>Evaluating the function at $t=3,$ we get</p>\n<p>\\begin{align*}\n\\mathbf r(3)\n&=\\left\\langle \\cos\\!\\left(\\dfrac{3\\pi}{2}\\right),\\, \\dfrac{4}{3-1} \\right\\rangle \\\\[5pt]\n&=\\left\\langle 0,\\,2 \\right\\rangle\n\\end{align*}</p>\n<p>Computing the magnitude of this vector, we obtain</p>\n<p>\\begin{align*}\n\\left|\\mathbf r(3)\\right|\n&= \\sqrt{0^2+2^2} \\\\[5pt]\n&=\\sqrt{4} \\\\[5pt]\n&=\\bbox[4pt,border: 1px solid lightgray]{2}\n\\end{align*}</p>\n","topic":{"id":475,"name":"Defining Vector-Valued Functions"},"example":{"id":12451,"title":"Finding the Magnitude of a Vector-Valued Function"},"group":{"id":8809,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14253258,"answer":{"id":62316341,"cread":"2026-10-16T02:53:42.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":null,"freeResponse":["4"],"timeElapsed":27584},"graphic":false,"freeResponse":{"segments":[{"newline":true},{"text":"$\\left|\\mathbf r(3)\\right| = $\n"},